    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters 2026-08-12 with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear offensive anchor. Facing Ryan Feltner (4.96 xERA), **Corbin Carroll** boasts an elite 87.14 daily score, fueled by a massive +19% SP skill advantage and a prime #2 lineup spot. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is a high-upside play at 75.75; while he hits lower in the order, he enjoys a massive +14% dynamic platoon advantage against Merrill Kelly, who has been susceptible to lefties this season. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang** round out our top-tier plays, both benefiting from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs near 5.00, providing the high-floor production we need to climb the standings.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Max Muncy**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 40.98 score. While he benefits from a positive park factor, the optimizer docked him heavily for facing the disciplined arm of Drew Rasmussen and the low-leverage #8 spot in the lineup. Conversely, we are keeping **Zach McKinstry** in the mix at 47.30; although his raw projection is lower than **Max Muncy**, his inclusion is a strategic hedge on stolen base scarcity, as his matchup against Foster Griffin offers a specialized situational edge for the base-path speed we covet.\n\nRisk management remains critical as every player in our lineup is currently marked as \"Lineup Pending.\" We are banking on **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang** hitting at the top of their respective orders to maximize their utility. We are also monitoring **Tyler Soderstrom** closely; while his score of 57.87 is solid, he faces the toughest pitcher of the day in Drew Rasmussen (3.17 xERA). If the confirmed lineups shuffle our order assumptions\u2014particularly for **Austin Riley** or **Zach McKinstry**\u2014we may face a drop in expected efficiency, but for now, the data suggests this aggressive construction provides the best path to maximizing our 5x5 totals. **James Wood** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active depth to fill the void.",
